pth_limit": 0, "concurrency_limit": 0, "budget": 0}, "by_type": {"implementer": 1}}, "safety_stops": 0, "is_error": false, "num_turns": 2, "subtype": "success", "api_error_status": null, "result": "The shell store is now made when `web/src/bridge.ts` loads, so an update status published at startup is no longer lost until a reload.\n\nThe implementer made the change, and I read the diff and reran the checks myself:\n- **Code:** `startShellStore()` sits right after `storeOfGlobal()` and returns it. It is called once at module level, right after its definition. The doc comments on `shellStore` and `useShell` now say the store is made at start. Nothing else in the file changed.\n- **Tests:** `pnpm --dir web test` passed in the implementer's run, 586 tests including the new case in `bridge.test.ts`. My rerun's output was cut off before the pass count, so I didn't see that summary myself.\n- **Types and lint:** `pnpm --dir web exec tsc -b` and `pnpm --dir web lint` both passed on my rerun.\n\nI didn't run the `uv` checks or the desktop app, since the spec lists only the web commands.", "ttft_ms": 1317, "type": "result", "duration_ms": 11937, "uuid": "1e3a21a8-4df8-42fe-9b20-494dbfc06d0f", "ttft_stream_ms": 969, "time_to_request_ms": 27, "first_content_frame_ms": 969, "queued_turn_count": 0, "result_index": 1}
